            <path d="M230 338 L238 470 L240 500 C240 518 230 525 218 525 L202 525 L198 500 L190 470 L185 338" fill="rgba(45,106,79,0.10)" stroke="#2d6a4f" stroke-width="1"></path>
            <text x="148" y="490" font-family="system-ui" font-size="9" fill="#2d6a4f" font-weight="500" text-anchor="middle">Leg</text>
            <text x="212" y="490" font-family="system-ui" font-size="9" fill="#2d6a4f" font-weight="500" text-anchor="middle">Leg</text>
          </g>
          <g class="region" data-region="foot" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Foot region">
            <rect x="122" y="525" width="48" height="24" rx="8" fill="rgba(45,106,79,0.10)" stroke="#2d6a4f" stroke-width="1"></rect>
            <text x="146" y="541" font-family="system-ui" font-size="9" fill="#2d6a4f" font-weight="500" text-anchor="middle">Foot</text>
            <rect x="190" y="525" width="48" height="24" rx="8" fill="rgba(45,106,79,0.10)" stroke="#2d6a4f" stroke-width="1"></rect>
            <text x="214" y="541" font-family="system-ui" font-size="9" fill="#2d6a4f" font-weight="500" text-anchor="middle">Foot</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <p class="text-center text-xs text-stone-400 mt-2">Tap or click a region</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="min-h-[480px]">
      <div id="pain-panels">
        <Fragment set:html={panelsHtml} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-3">How to Use This Map</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed">
      <li>Start where it hurts: tap the matching body region to see what commonly causes that discomfort and which acupressure points are worth trying.</li>
      <li>Read the <span class="text-red-600 dark:text-red-400 font-medium">"See a doctor if"</span> list first. Acupressure is for everyday tension and minor discomfort — it is not a substitute for medical care.</li>
      <li>Click any point card to open the full guide with exact location, how to press, and how long to hold.</li>
      <li>If you feel pain in several regions at once, the condition guides (headache, back pain, sleep, anxiety, nausea) show complete routines that combine points across the body.</li>
      <li>Prefer browsing by anatomy? The <a href="/atlas/" class="text-emerald-700 hover:underline dark:text-emerald-400">interactive atlas</a> organizes the same twelve regions with point location guides.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-3">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <details class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-stone-800 dark:bg-stone-900 mb-3"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Is this a medical diagnostic tool?</summary><div class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">No. It maps common everyday causes of pain and the red-flag symptoms that need a doctor's attention, based on how acupressure practitioners and primary care generally categorize these complaints. It cannot replace an examination.</div></details>
    <details class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-stone-800 dark:bg-stone-900 mb-3"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Why does the map show the back as the opposite side?</summary><div class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">The most important back points sit along the Bladder meridian in two lines beside the spine, so the back is drawn separately with a dashed outline for clarity.</div></details>
    <details class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-stone-800 dark:bg-stone-900 mb-3"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">I have chest pain. Should I press a point?</summary><div class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">If chest pain comes with sweating, shortness of breath, or pain spreading to the jaw or arm, seek emergency care immediately — do not delay to try acupressure. For mild stress-related tightness, the chest region guide shows gentle points, and the anxiety guide offers a full routine.</div></details>
    <details class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-stone-800 dark:bg-stone-900"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Which region should a beginner start with?</summary><div class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">The hand and foot regions. Their points are easy to find and reach, and they cover common needs such as headaches, nausea, stress, and sleep.</div></details>
  </section>
</div>
<script is:inline>
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
    var regions = document.querySelectorAll('.region[data-region]');
    var panels = document.querySelectorAll('[data-region-panel]');
    var active = null;

    function select(key, scroll) {
      if (active === key) return;
      active = key;
      regions.forEach(function (r) {
        var on = r.getAttribute('data-region') === key;
        r.classList.toggle('region-active', on);
        r.setAttribute('aria-pressed', on ? 'true' : 'false');
      });
      panels.forEach(function (p) {
        p.classList.toggle('hidden', p.getAttribute('data-region-panel') !== key);
      });
      if (scroll) {
        var panel = document.querySelector('[data-region-panel="' + key + '"]');
        var rect = panel.getBoundingClientRect();
        if (rect.top < 0) { panel.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' }); }
      }
    }

    regions.forEach(function (r) {
      r.style.cursor = 'pointer';
      r.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false');
      r.addEventListener('click', function () { select(this.getAttribute('data-region'), true); });
      r.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
        if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ') { e.preventDefault(); select(this.getAttribute('data-region'), true); }
      });
    });

    var first = document.querySelector('[data-region]');
    if (first) select(first.getAttribute('data-region'), false);
  });
</script>
<style>
  .region { transition: opacity 0.15s ease; }
  .region-active > ellipse, .region-active > rect, .region-active > path { filter: url(#glow); stroke-width: 2.5 !important; }
  .region-active > text { font-weight: 700 !important; }
  .region:not(.region-active) { opacity: 0.75; }
  .region:hover, .region:focus-visible { outline: none; }
  .region:hover > ellipse, .region:hover > rect, .region:hover > path, .region:focus-visible > ellipse, .region:focus-visible > rect, .region:focus-visible > path { stroke-width: 2.5; }
</style>
</BaseLayout>